\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces  Total energy convergence (left $y$ axis) and force convergence (right $y$ axis) during the relaxation test run of H$_2$O. A total of five steps is taken (initial geometry plus four relaxation steps). The total energy of the final step is taken as the reference here, and the total energy in the second-to-last step is already identical within the numerical accuracy of the calculation. The final step is only taken to bring the residual forces (total energy gradients) to practically zero as well. \relax }}{288}{figure.caption.95}}
\newlabel{Fig:H2O-relaxation}{{4.1}{288}{Total energy convergence (left $y$ axis) and force convergence (right $y$ axis) during the relaxation test run of H$_2$O. A total of five steps is taken (initial geometry plus four relaxation steps). The total energy of the final step is taken as the reference here, and the total energy in the second-to-last step is already identical within the numerical accuracy of the calculation. The final step is only taken to bring the residual forces (total energy gradients) to practically zero as well. \relax }{figure.caption.95}{}}
